_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 90
---
order: 90
---
short_label: X.90
---
statement: To find the sixth apotome.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Set out a rational straight line *A*, and set out three numbers *E*, *BC*, and *CD* not having to one another the ratio which a square number has to a square number, and further let *CB* also not have to *BD* the ratio which a square number has to a square number.

Let it be contrived that *E* is to *BC* as the square on *A* is to the square on *FG*, and *BC* is to *CD* as the square on *FG* is to the square on *GH*. [!just X.6.Cor]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="240" height="195" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.90 diagram" src="propX90.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
